cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "From Molecules to Quantum Circuits: A Practical Guide to Fermion-to-Qubit Encodings"
authors:
  - family-names: Azariah
    given-names: John S
    orcid: ""
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-03-09"
url: "https://github.com/johnazariah/encodings-book"
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnazariah/encodings-book"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum chemistry
  - fermion-to-qubit encoding
  - Jordan-Wigner
  - Bravyi-Kitaev
  - Trotterization
  - qubit tapering
  - FockMap
abstract: >-
  A self-contained 22-chapter guide covering the complete pipeline from
  molecular electronic structure to quantum circuit compilation. Includes
  five fermionic encodings, qubit tapering, Trotter decomposition, circuit
  export, and computed results (H₂ dissociation curve, H₂O bond angle scan).
  Companion labs provide interactive F# scripts using the FockMap library.
